    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on a high-ceiling performance from **Josh Naylor** (77.77) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Zack Littell and Tatsuya Imai, respectively. Both sluggers enjoy an 18-19% SP skill boost, with **Josh Naylor** further aided by a 5% platoon advantage against the right-handed Littell. **Corbin Carroll** (71.85) remains a mandatory start due to his elite sprint speed and volume profile, even with a slight negative platoon adjustment against Nick Lodolo. **Brice Turang** (66.63) also presents a strong play, as the optimizer prioritizes his stolen base potential despite the marginal speed bump presented by an elite defensive catcher.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves **Max Muncy** (53.84), who finished just shy of the threshold to displace **Dalton Rushing** or **Alex Freeland**. While **Max Muncy** provides a stable floor, the optimizer favored **Dalton Rushing** due to the favorable 4.78 xERA matchup against Anthony Kay, where the potential for high-impact plate appearances outweighs the static projection. Owners should keep a close eye on weather and final lineup confirmations, as **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young** are currently calculated based on assumed orderings. Should any of these players move down the lineup, their efficiency scores\u2014particularly for **Alex Freeland** (54.08), who is already suffering an 8% penalty for batting ninth\u2014could plummet, necessitating a pivot to **Austin Riley** (46.70) or **Travis Bazzana** (48.68) if late-breaking information shifts the platoon environment.",
